From dd9dd41d168c16e1a70e45b5b36a79a746781942 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 20:15:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(app): judge only axial lathe holes by the axial-hole
 verdict

`lathe_axial` was true for any lathe Drill, so the axial verdict
(`drilling::axial_warnings`, which convicts any chain without canned
cycles) judged every lathe cross drill's radial path and blocked it
("move 1 cuts past the finish surface"). It now holds only for a lathe
Drill with no cross holes; the cross arm keeps its own laws (spindle,
raw-stock standoffs and rapid proof, reach and holder, radial rapids),
none of which read `lathe_axial`. Mixed lists stay refused by name.

Fixes #80

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
